---
import ProjectLayout from '../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import CaseImage from '../../../components/CaseImage.astro';
import okeDashboard from '../../../assets/case-studies/oke-dashboard.png';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Multi-cluster OKE with GitOps"
  description="Multi-cluster Kubernetes (OKE) architecture with continuous delivery via ArgoCD, and a systematic diagnostic pattern for production failures."
  domain="kubernetes"
  caseId="02"
>
  <h2>Context</h2>
  <p>
    Multiple teams and products running on separate OKE clusters (production and staging/review),
    each with several namespaces (APIs, portal, RPAs, whitelabel). Without a single deployment
    standard, each namespace evolved with its own practices — which made auditing harder and slowed
    down incident diagnosis.
  </p>

  <h2>Approach</h2>
  <p>
    Standardization via GitOps: ArgoCD watching repositories on Bitbucket, with templated manifests
    (<strong>app.yml.tpl</strong>) versioned per environment. The normal flow is: an immediate fix
    via <code>kubectl</code> when something breaks in production, followed by committing the fix to the
    template — ensuring the next automatic <em>sync</em> doesn't reintroduce the problem.
  </p>

  <h2>Systematic diagnosis</h2>
  <p>Over time, a clear root-cause pattern emerged for the main pod failure states:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>CrashLoopBackOff / CreateContainerConfigError</strong> — almost always tied to malformed
      secrets (using <code>stringData</code> vs. direct base64, or a residual newline introduced by <code
        >echo</code
      > without the <code>-n</code> flag).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>ImagePullBackOff</strong> — usually an outdated image tag or an expired registry token.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Port mismatch</strong> — the most recurring and easiest-to-prevent cause: Node.js apps defaulting
      to port 3333, .NET defaulting to 8080, while the Service/Deployment pointed to a different port.
      Today this is part of a checklist before any new deploy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Auto-sync conflicts</strong> — stale <code>last-applied-configuration</code>{' '}
      annotations causing ArgoCD to detect "drift" where there wasn't any, requiring manual annotation
      cleanup for the sync to stabilize.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <CaseImage
    src={okeDashboard}
    alt="Grafana dashboard showing running pods, pending pods, failed pods, and CPU/memory usage per node and per namespace on an OKE cluster"
    caption="Grafana dashboard consuming cluster metrics — running/failed pods, resource usage per node and per namespace. Internal identifiers have been removed."
  />

  <h2>Result</h2>
  <p>
    Reduced average diagnosis time for deployment incidents, trivial rollback via{' '}
    <code>git revert</code>, and a clear audit trail of who changed what in each environment —
    something the previous manual operation didn't offer.
  </p>
</ProjectLayout>
